# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Instructions

**The single entry point.** Every other document is reached from here, and this file
decides what must be read before a given task. If you are an agent or a new
contributor, start here and nowhere else.

Owned by whoever owns the codebase. Must change whenever a document is added,
renamed, or retired — a router that points at a moved file is worse than no router,
because it is still trusted.

---

## 1. Mandatory rules

<!-- DECIDE: these are the rules that override everything else. Keep the list
     short enough that people actually remember it. Four to eight is realistic. -->

1. Read this file before writing any code.
2. Before any documentation change, read the documentation-rules document — its
   rules override all other instructions.
3. Before any PR action, read the PR document and follow it exactly.
4. If a request conflicts with a project document, **flag the conflict** and ask.
   Never silently ignore a documented rule.
5. When an architectural or design decision is made, update the relevant document
   as part of the same change — not as a follow-up.

## 2. Reading order

The rules above are universal. **What to read next is not** — it depends on what this
project is. Fill in the row that applies and delete the others, then keep the result
as this project's actual reading order.

